  "candidates": [
    {
      "mechanism": "Server-local calendar window changes the native low-light Bat placement random gate; resting is downstream.",
      "evidence": [
        "EntityType puts Bat in AMBIENT, and SpawnPlacements registers ON_GROUND with MOTION_BLOCKING_NO_LEAVES. NaturalSpawner checks the placement type before its NATURAL predicate and then separately checks collision and entity-level validity. A flying body does not determine the native placement enum.",
        "Bat.checkBatSpawnRules rejects Y at or above level sea level. Below sea level, LocalDate.now() uses the JVM default zone and Oct 20 through Nov 3 inclusive selects nextInt(7). Outside that window nextBoolean can reject first, followed by nextInt(4). Both require raw brightness no greater than the sampled integer and then reach Mob.checkMobSpawnRules.",
        "For NATURAL the inherited final floor predicate checks the block beneath the candidate. The Forge SpawnPlacementCheck result can override the registered predicate result after evaluation; the native physical placement gate precedes it.",
        "The bound base forest, dripstone caves and ocean ambient tables list Bat with weight 10 and nominal group 8. The bound deep dark table has no Bat entry. NaturalSpawner samples the group bounds, but its independent attempt counter checks the Forge pack-size result, which defaults to the inherited Bat limit of 4 and can be overridden. Group-table data alone yields neither a realized group nor a server spawn rate.",
        "A server Bat starts resting. A nearby player or loss of the conductive ceiling can end the rest, and the flying branch can return to rest beneath a conductive ceiling. The resting flag persists. A later roost location or resting observation does not identify the original spawn block."
      ],
      "branch_math": {
        "conditioning": "Fixed below-sea-level site reaching the Bat callback, final floor predicate allowed, default event behavior. Values describe only the two local random branches.",
